  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a connected, undirected graph consisting of NNN nodes and MMM edges. Every node has a pass value of AiA_iAi​ and a monster with health BiB_iBi​.\n\nYour task is to defeat all the monsters eventually. To do that, you can do the following steps:\n\n\nChoose a starting node SSS (1≤S≤N1 \\le S \\le N1≤S≤N) and a starting health value HHH.\nSuppose your current node is XXX, you can either battle the monster (if it has not been fought already) or go to a different node. Both the actions have some restrictions. Specifically,\n\nIf you choose to battle the monster, H≥BXH \\ge B_XH≥BX​ must hold. After fighting this monster, your health changes to H−BXH - B_XH−BX​.\nIf you choose to go to a different node YYY, there must be an edge between XXX and YYY. Further, your health must be greater than the pass values of both nodes XXX and YYY, i.e. H≥AXH \\ge A_XH≥AX​ and H≥AYH \\ge A_YH≥AY​.\n\n\nFind the minimum possible starting health value HHH such that it is possible to beat all monsters. You may choose to start at any node.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and MMM — the number of vertices and edges of the graph, respectively.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,...,ANA_1, A_2, ..., A_NA1​,A2​,...,AN​, the pass values of each node.\nThe third line contains NNN integers - B1,B2,...,BNB_1, B_2, ..., B_NB1​,B2​,...,BN​, the monster healths of each node.\nThe next MMM lines describe the edges. The iii-th of these MMM lines contains two space-separated integers uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​, denoting an edge between uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum starting health value.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "N−1≤M≤min⁡(N⋅(N−1)2,2⋅105)N - 1 \\le M \\le \\min(\\frac{N \\cdot (N - 1)}{2}, 2 \\cdot 10^5)N−1≤M≤min(2N⋅(N−1)​,2⋅105)",
      "1≤Ai,Bi≤1091 \\le A_i, B_i \\le 10^91≤Ai​,Bi​≤109",
      "1≤ui,vi≤N1 \\le u_i, v_i \\le N1≤ui​,vi​≤N",
      "ui≠viu_i \\ne v_iui​=vi​",
      "All the MMM unordered pairs (ui,vi)(u_i, v_i)(ui​,vi​) are different.",
      "The sum of NNN and the sum of MMM both do not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105 over all test cases."
    ],
